{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_evidence_schema_evidencepayload", "label": "EvidencePayload envelope", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The union is closed and discriminated so a payload whose data does not match its eventType is rejected rather than written, and Zod strips undeclared keys so a leaked field does not survive parsing. Where the doc and the Zod schemas disagree, the schemas win."}, {"id": "docs_evidence_schema_canonical_json", "label": "lib/canonical-json.ts key ordering rule", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keys sorted by code unit, array order preserved, undefined dropped, and anything JSON cannot round-trip rejected outright; hashes stored as bare 64-hex so every link including the all-zero genesis has the same shape."}, {"id": "docs_evidence_schema_pii_rule", "label": "The PII rule for evidence payloads", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every field must be an identifier, an enum, a score or a hash \u2014 that is the test to apply before adding one."}, {"id": "docs_evidence_schema_payee_consent_event", "label": "payee_consent evidence event", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ordered before match and decision because it authorises them: a chain showing a match with no consent ahead of it describes a system with no gate. The consent signature stays on the PayeeConsent row, since a second copy in an anchored structure buys nothing a dispute needs."}, {"id": "docs_evidence_schema_world_id_check_event", "label": "world_id_check evidence event", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_evidence_schema_vendor_match_event", "label": "vendor_match evidence event", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kept as a separate record from decision, in causal order: one combined record would lose the distinction between 'the match was wrong' and 'the policy was wrong'."}, {"id": "docs_evidence_schema_decision_event", "label": "decision evidence event", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_evidence_schema_evidence_accessed_event", "label": "evidence_accessed self-audit event", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reading the audit trail is itself audited; appendStandalone is the one non-transactional append and retries on a unique-constraint collision because two concurrent readers can race for the same chain tip."}, {"id": "docs_evidence_schema_write_rule", "label": "Same-transaction append rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EvidenceService.append takes a transaction client precisely so there is deliberately no 'append later' method."}, {"id": "docs_evidence_schema_chain_verification", "label": "Chain verification on read (content vs linkage break)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recomputed from genesis on every read rather than trusting a stored flag, reporting the first break with its index and distinguishing a payload that no longer hashes to its stored hash from a record that does not link to its predecessor."}, {"id": "docs_evidence_schema_nullifier_omission", "label": "World ID nullifier never written to the chain", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The nullifier is a stable per-person identifier within an action, so publishing it would let anyone holding two records link the same human across payments."}, {"id": "docs_evidence_schema_vendor_level_gap", "label": "Gap: vendor-level events have no evidence chain", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "EvidenceRecord requires a paymentRequestId, so identity-verified, wallet-confirmed and KYB-status-changed events are unrecorded; needs either a nullable payment reference or a separate vendor chain."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_evidence_schema_evidencepayload", "target": "docs_architecture_evidence_hash_chain", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evidence_schema_pii_rule", "target": "docs_architecture_no_pii_on_chain", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/evidence-schema.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_evidence_schema_write_rule", "target": "docs_architecture_evidence_record_per_action", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.